  data: {
    LLM: "Pure luck. There is no strategy in card selection since it's random. The strategy is in money management and reading opponents for side bets. If you see two 7s already gone, betting heavily on a 7 is safer (only one 7 left means less chance of falling soon? No, wait. If 2 7s are gone, there are 2 left in deck. Probability of falling is lower than if 3 were left? Yes. But eventually it must fall if you play to end of deck).\n\nThe 'Turn': Watch the turn cards. If a card hasn't appeared for a long time (is 'sleeping'), it's due. Gambler's fallacy, but common in Skin logic.\n\nBankroll Management: In a fair game, variance will kill you. Don't bet everything on one card. Spread bets across multiple cards if allowed (playing two hands).",
    Player: "Pure luck. There is no strategy in card selection since it's random. The strategy is in money management and reading opponents for side bets. If you see two 7s already gone, betting heavily on a 7 is safer (only one 7 left means less chance of falling soon? No, wait. If 2 7s are gone, there are 2 left in deck. Probability of falling is lower than if 3 were left? Yes. But eventually it must fall if you play to end of deck).\n\nThe 'Turn': Watch the turn cards. If a card hasn't appeared for a long time (is 'sleeping'), it's due. Gambler's fallacy, but common in Skin logic.\n\nBankroll Management: In a fair game, variance will kill you. Don't bet everything on one card. Spread bets across multiple cards if allowed (playing two hands).",
